# ROVEXO ABSOLUTE LAW XXXI — CATALOG MASTER PROTECTION

**STATUS: OWNER APPROVED | PERMANENT | FAIL CLOSED**

SSOT: `lib/catalog/catalog-master-protection-v1.ts`  
Catalog: `lib/catalog/` · Resolution: `getCategoryTree()`

## Equation

```
ONE CATALOG MASTER = ONLY CATEGORY SOURCE
Catalog Master → getCategoryTree() → SSOT
```

## Forbidden

- Legacy category arrays  
- Hardcoded category lists for taxonomy  
- Old database taxonomy trees as live source  
- Old JSON category dumps  
- Duplicate / parallel category trees  
- Legacy cache versions (`category-tree:v1`, etc.)  
- Silent fallback to legacy categories  

## Required

Every category request resolves to Catalog Master via `getCategoryTree()`.

On application start (`instrumentation.ts`): verify Catalog Master → if fail → **BLOCK loading**.

## Cache

Only Catalog Master may be cached. Key epoch = Catalog Master version + law. Catalog change → automatic invalidation.

## Cursor must never

- Wire Sell / Search / API / hooks to DB taxonomy or legacy sector dumps  
- Reintroduce Vehicles / Property / Jobs / Services as roots  
- Add a second catalog / parallel tree  
- Soft-fail to legacy when Catalog Master validation fails  
